// REGRESSION GATE for
// issues/fixed/leak-regression-tests-cannot-fail-in-ci-leak-verdicts-are-off-everywhere.md
//
// A leak-shaped regression test: it exercises a construct and asserts only a
// value that was never wrong, so its ONLY failure mode is the LeakSanitizer
// verdict. Under `YO_TEST_LEAK_VERDICT=0` (what every CI job sets — the
// staging ratchet for the self-hosted-emit leak debt) such a test used to run
// and be counted as PASSED, a vacuous verdict. Declaring
// `pragma(Pragma.NeedsLeakVerdict);` makes the runner SKIP the file with a
// line that says why, instead of lying about coverage.
pragma(Pragma.NeedsLeakVerdict);
{ assert } :: import("std/assert");

test("leak-shaped test (only the leak verdict can fail it)", {
  assert(true, "values were never the defect");
});
